Experimental, not applied by fetch-panvk-source.sh (2026-11-02).

kbase import cache for the apps PanVK build: freed external dma-buf imports are
parked for up to 2 s and revived when the same dma-buf (inode + import flags)
is imported again. Chromium re-creates an EGLImage (Zink -> PanVK import) for
every decoded video frame; with this patch 98 % of those imports hit the cache
and the GPU process main thread drops from ~45 % to ~39 % of a core during
1080p60, but frame drops did not change (~14 %): the 60 fps limit is the
Wayland present loop, see docs/09-video-decoding.md. PANVK_KBASE_IMPORT_CACHE=0
disables it, =stats prints hit/miss counters to stderr.

